Here's a simple function that searches a HTML table for a given phrase:
```javascript
function searchTable(tableId, phrase) {
  // Get the table element
  var table = document.getElementById(tableId);

  // Loop through each table row (tr)
  for (var i = 0; i < table.rows.length; i++) {
    // Get the text contents of the current row's cells
    var rowText = table.rows[i].textContent;

    // Check if the row's text contains the given phrase
    if (rowText.toLowerCase().indexOf(phrase.toLowerCase()) > -1) {
      // If it does, add a class to the row to highlight it
      table.rows[i].classList.add('highlight');
    }
  }
}
```
To use this function, you would pass in the ID of the table you want to search and the phrase you want to search for. For example:
```javascript
searchTable('my-table', 'table');
```
This would search the table with the ID `my-table` for the string `table` and highlight any rows that contain that string. You can customize the function to fit your specific needs, such as searching for a phrase in multiple columns or adding a callback function to handle the results.
